  "studyDescription": "These values were generated for teaching; they are not measurements from a real survey, and no students were asked. They are modelled on a class survey in which 62 introductory statistics students report how many hours they exercise in a typical week, rounded to the nearest half hour, with 34 reporting female and 28 male. The distribution is right-skewed, as self-reported exercise usually is: most students report a few hours a week and a few report a great deal.",
  "variableDescriptions": {
    "sex": "The sex a student reported, female or male.",
    "exercise_hours": "Hours of exercise in a typical week, as the student reported it, rounded to the nearest half hour."
  },
  "sourceDetail": "Simulated data, generated by StatLens (2026-10-03) for a two-sample comparison of means. Built to be realistic in shape and size rather than to reproduce any particular study. Use it to practise the procedure and the wording of a conclusion; for a real two-group comparison of means see births14_smoke, stem_cell or lizard_run.",
  "context": {
    "population": "introductory statistics students",
    "parameter": "the difference in mean weekly exercise hours between male and female students",
    "unit": "hours per week"
  },
